From b43ddddfc81f64ee70c4a2bd818aa0a9e05406da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: casablanque-code <casablanque@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 06:02:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] merge dashboard into railcast-api: one Worker, one domain
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two Workers (railcast-api + railcast-dashboard) meant CORS, a
cross-subdomain session cookie, and two separate Workers Builds
configs for what is really one app on one domain.

Instead: the dashboard's static export (dashboard/out) is served
directly by railcast-api via Workers static assets ([assets] in
worker/wrangler.toml, directory = "../dashboard/out", resolved
relative to the config file so it works regardless of deploy cwd).
Static files are matched first; anything else (/api/*, /auth/*,
/:appId/appcast.xml, uploads) falls through to the Worker script.

- worker: drop CORS_ORIGIN entirely (same-origin now, no preflight
  ever happens); session cookie loses its Domain attribute and
  redirects become relative ("/", "/dashboard")
- worker: /dashboard route removed from the router — it's a real
  static file now, served before the Worker script ever runs;
  /login kept as a compat redirect to "/" for old bookmarks
- dashboard: lib/api.ts defaults to relative paths; drop the
  wrangler dependency, deploy script, and dashboard/wrangler.toml
  (no separate deploy step anymore)
- verified with 'wrangler deploy --dry-run' from worker/: picks up
  all 31 files from ../dashboard/out plus the D1/R2 bindings
- typecheck + full vitest suite still green (12/12)
- README: corrected deploy instructions (build dashboard first,
  then wrangler deploy from worker/) and Workers Builds settings
  for the single-Worker setup
